#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166603 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6e692dca-1bbc-59e7-999f-4acb806ddd38" :question/math-academy-id "e-8369" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =7\\arcsch(1-x),$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcsch x) = -\\dfrac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =7\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =7(-\\frac{1}{|1-x|\\sqrt{1+(1-x)^{2}}})\\cdot (1-x)^{′} \\\\  & =7(-\\frac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{1+1-2x+{x}^{2}}})\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{|x-1|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2x+2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166604 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b4dd5d1a-eeae-58f5-b7a1-a6a20fb02df9" :question/math-academy-id "e-8370" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =  5\\arsech{2x},$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arsech x) = -\\dfrac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\\\  & =5(-\\frac{1}{(2x)\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}})\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166605 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/id #uuid "83b6c061-a8fc-5628-a199-60196b904407" :question/math-academy-id "e-8371" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y = \\arcoth{e^x},$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcoth x) = \\dfrac{1}{1-x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-({e}^{x})^{2}}\\cdot ({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{2x}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1-{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166606 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5e40340-35cf-50ee-8a0d-7eb873490693" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "8a1806e8-d99d-5107-aa63-0bf841cb44c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-8372" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $f(x) = \\sin{x} \\cdot \\arcsch{x},$ then $f'(x) = \\cos{x} \\arcsch{x} + g(x).$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIn this case, the expression for $f(x)$  is a product $u(x) \\cdot v(x)$ with $u(x) = \\sin{x}$ and $v(x) = \\arcsch{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+{{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}})}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x) = -\\dfrac{\\sin{x}}{|x|\\sqrt{1+x^2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f577fac-247a-5f5a-8564-52657ee5b19a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2x+2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f577fac-247a-5f5a-8564-52657ee5b19a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2x+2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519227} :answer-field/id #uuid "5de9fb92-f20f-5c9e-9ed0-941e3ef44838" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6edfa6ba-1072-5bf1-bdfe-2aaa6d5af318" :question/math-academy-id "q-341457" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(x-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{|x-1|}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[3\\,\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(x-1)] \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(x-1)] \\\\  & =3\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{1+(x-1)^{2}}}]\\cdot (x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{|x-1|\\sqrt{1+({x}^{2}-2x+1)}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|x-1|}\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2x+2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4444a1b2-e52a-551a-af2f-64eee4dc99a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8x^3}{\\sqrt{1+(x^4+2)^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4444a1b2-e52a-551a-af2f-64eee4dc99a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8x^3}{\\sqrt{1+(x^4+2)^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519097} :answer-field/id #uuid "cee78980-cb6b-5efb-8a9d-827bb3ab4617" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519495}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a0460884-e620-5591-b0cf-266181de3168" :question/math-academy-id "q-341470" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{4}+2),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}+2}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{4}+2)] \\\\  & =2\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{|{x}^{4}+2|\\sqrt{1+{({x}^{4}+2)}^{2}}}]\\cdot {({x}^{4}+2)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{({x}^{4}+2)\\sqrt{1+({x}^{8}+4{x}^{4}+4)}}\\cdot 4{x}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}+2}\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{8}+4{x}^{4}+5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fa9e367-921c-5703-b5c8-f4ef0ec283c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fa9e367-921c-5703-b5c8-f4ef0ec283c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519228} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b26d762-7065-5240-845a-7fa72921023d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519462}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24bbcf4d-e35e-5166-86db-6c3a81f4f4ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-341493" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-3\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[-3\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x)] \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x)] \\\\  & =-3\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}}]\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fb02d74-74dc-50e4-a17f-f8ce53c1c0a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(x-1)\\sqrt{\\,x(2-x)\\,}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fb02d74-74dc-50e4-a17f-f8ce53c1c0a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(x-1)\\sqrt{\\,x(2-x)\\,}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519017} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2e24b88-1d44-5062-9037-62a3b48a7fe6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db2fa4fe-6b60-51ee-9a41-fc33e6f273b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-341497" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-4\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(x-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-4\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(x-1)] \\\\  & =-4\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{(x-1)\\sqrt{1-(x-1)^{2}}}]\\cdot (x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(x-1)\\sqrt{1-({x}^{2}-2x+1)}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(x-1)\\sqrt{2x-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(x-1)\\sqrt{\\,x(2-x)\\,}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167345 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a7c01f1-d39c-5196-9258-c0eec7c07444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519060} {:answer/id #uuid "40c362a9-19d5-5d8c-a4a3-3cf9958ccbe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519094} {:answer/id #uuid "71eb7122-dc51-5d2b-9bdd-e41da71e7ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519164} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf13911-5554-5451-9cf9-4e74b60ef167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519302} {:answer/id #uuid "fd0e91da-cb8a-5d7b-991b-d2333882fbdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71eb7122-dc51-5d2b-9bdd-e41da71e7ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519164} :answer-field/id #uuid "483dd5ca-6b7d-5085-88c4-f59f04b7faf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5e2b948-b294-5c79-aebf-65f70417475a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95318" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{x}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}|\\sqrt{1+({x}^{2})^{2}}}\\cdot ({x}^{2})^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x\\sqrt{1+{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05978ef2-526e-513b-a296-30e858ad7d1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{x\\sqrt{1+9{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518996} {:answer/id #uuid "6bab7b0e-c8aa-5da1-a567-dc2e839c9038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-3{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519151} {:answer/id #uuid "871baed0-e9b4-51b3-b72c-1009d740fb54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4x\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519206} {:answer/id #uuid "9582718d-5732-5f67-8454-d0600cb51fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1+3{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519239} {:answer/id #uuid "9f294f0d-3335-520f-be6a-4f7a8