}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519076} {:answer/id #uuid "54d6cd33-d4de-58b7-8f64-738c8128b497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{1+16{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519123} {:answer/id #uuid "85e270b6-45ce-567e-9271-f69abcdff687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{1+16{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519203} {:answer/id #uuid "d06920a3-ba34-58db-ba10-ad2913c12c48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4|x|\\sqrt{1+16{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519332} {:answer/id #uuid "db27974c-ad6f-568e-a27d-852868230ae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85e270b6-45ce-567e-9271-f69abcdff687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{1+16{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519203} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0359eb2-a7b5-51ab-a406-e6a8025c07cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e70aada-1f44-5184-b986-16d8ac2cfc36" :question/math-academy-id "q-95503" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-3\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡4x,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡4x) \\\\  & =-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡4x) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|4x|\\sqrt{1+(4x)^{2}}})\\cdot (4x)^{′} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{4|x|\\sqrt{1+16{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{1+16{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519603 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35a0d67f-2001-5b60-b42a-f979cd7b3038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{4x}(1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519074} {:answer/id #uuid "753c754d-a64b-5a86-bf3d-b11e9cb247e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519175} {:answer/id #uuid "762e2957-2bdc-5c9f-8c82-28884cca64d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({e}^{4x}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519177} {:answer/id #uuid "a25c36b2-66bd-5740-89f4-e95b59786f40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{2x}({e}^{2x}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519258} {:answer/id #uuid "c60203e4-de60-549e-8d11-366f51f688e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{4x}(1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "753c754d-a64b-5a86-bf3d-b11e9cb247e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519175} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac258ea5-31b3-5f32-97e0-aac682319621" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7c92bc5-8061-56c3-9e0d-1e01c4282d73" :question/math-academy-id "q-95511" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y={e}^{4x}-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{e}^{2x},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{4x}-2\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{e}^{2x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{4x})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{e}^{2x}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x}-2(-\\frac{1}{|{e}^{2x}|\\sqrt{1+({e}^{2x})^{2}}})\\cdot ({e}^{2x})^{′} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x}+\\frac{2}{{e}^{2x}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}}\\cdot 2{e}^{2x} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}} \\\\  & =4({e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{4x}}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
